action: Reinforce across every scenario that local jurisdictional alerts, law-enforcement road closures, county evacuation maps, and live NWS/fire/hazmat directives ALWAYS supersede generalized encyclopedia guidance—no draft text predicts site-specific disaster safety. @D01,D14,D15
action: Maintain `publication: HOLD` and zero qualified human approvals across all 65 Z15 pages until qualified emergency-management directors, meteorologists, air-quality/public-health specialists, hazmat responders, and accessibility planners complete formal sign-off (`H13`). @D01,D06,ED
failure: Distributing unreviewed disaster-scenario drafts as official local emergency instructions without county/jurisdictional alignment or qualified specialist review. @D01,ED
verify: Confirm the primer reconstruction label is preserved, zero flood-driving or tornado-overpass errors exist, and `publication: HOLD` stays active on all 65 Z15 cards. @D05,D03,ED
stop: Do NOT lift `publication: HOLD` or merge into `main` until Astra technical audit and qualified hazard/emergency-management reviews are recorded in the custody ledger. @D01,ED
